00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.420
But usually I talk about topics

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.560
such as professional communication,

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.090
slide writing techniques,

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.300
and also problem solving skills.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.780
So, typical things that are
part of the consultant toolkit

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.227
that I do think many
students will benefit from,

00:03:08.227 --> 00:03:11.590
especially those with
a business background

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:12.760
that want to make their way

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.750
into professional
services like consulting.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.947
So this was also the focus of today

00:03:17.947 --> 00:03:21.320
with some many great
discussions, questions,

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.175
participation from the students,

00:03:23.175 --> 00:03:26.840
very high energy and engaging environment.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.280
It's a pleasure to be here now

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.070
with Vanessa, Patrick,
Hendrik and Marijan,

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:35.600
four master students at
the WHU here in Vallendar.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.730
So I'd love just to hear from all of you

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:41.160
what it's like to study at
such a private business school.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.660
It is indeed, I'd argue,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.080
probably the best business
school in Germany.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.157
So for sure, not your average student,

00:03:48.157 --> 00:03:50.440
with whom I'm surrounded here with,

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.330
but maybe let me hear from you.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.520
What is special about studying at WHU,

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.160
studying at such a private university?

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.420
Who wants to start?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.518
Maybe can (indistinct).

00:04:00.518 --> 00:04:01.351
- Oh, I can start for sure.

00:04:01.351 --> 00:04:02.380
Well, I think it's very special

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.230
that we are very close community.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.138
You are so close to your friends,

00:04:06.138 --> 00:04:07.460
you meet them every day,

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.110
and of course that's very
important for your future work.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.380
You will be connected for
the rest of your life.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.770
I think that's what makes it special.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.400
- Maybe another very interesting aspect

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.570
is actually the network, right?

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:24.296
It's amazing which type of
people we have here on campus,

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:25.787
be it as guest lecturers,

00:04:25.787 --> 00:04:29.816
or be it as parts of all
these different conferences.

00:04:29.816 --> 00:04:32.500
A very memorable moment for me

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.268
was when Kagan Sumer, the
CEO of Gorillas, was here

00:04:36.268 --> 00:04:40.817
and talked with us and explained
many different insights

00:04:40.817 --> 00:04:41.950
